---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { LinkButton } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";
import newToEsphomeImg from "../../assets/images/homepage/new-to-esphome.webp";
---

<section class="new-to-esphome card-bgc">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-container">
      <h2>New to ESPHome? Read this!</h2>
      <p>
        Every ESPHome device is built around a small, inexpensive chip called a microcontroller – commonly an ESP32
        (hence the name ESPHome!), but it also works with others like RP2040 or BK72xx. The chip is the programmable
        part that controls your sensors, switches, and displays. ESPHome generates the firmware (the internal software
        operating system) that runs on that chip to give it its instructions. Once installed, the chip can then “talk”
        directly to Home Assistant or any other smart home system that supports it.
      </p>

      <Image src={newToEsphomeImg} alt="New to ESPHome" layout="constrained" />

      <LinkButton href="/install/">Get started</LinkButton>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  @use "../../styles/mixins" as *;

  .new-to-esphome {
    img {
      max-height: 100%;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      @include fluid(16, 32, $property: margin-top);
      @include fluid(16, 32, $property: margin-bottom);
    }
  }
</style>
